## 2. Why this measurement is a discovery test, not a formality

**M-2's pre-registered NULL FAILED in the 2D channel at both venues.** The
overlap-stratified matched read (m2_results.json, verified CONFIRMED by
independent recompute, `m2_adjudication.json`) found:

| venue | channel | matched residual (nats/event) | matched signflip p | cluster-robust p | call |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| iiib | 1D | +0.00604 | 0.098 | 0.233 | NULL |
| iiib | 2D | **+0.02225** | 1.5e-04 | **0.0050** | **NON-NULL** |
| joint_r1 | 1D | +0.00743 | 0.0414 | 0.137 | marginal-fragile (effectively unresolved toward NULL) |
| joint_r1 | 2D | **+0.02070** | 1.0e-04 | **0.0042** | **NON-NULL** |

Chord sign convention: `chord = ln L(0.60) − ln L(0.73)`; positive = event
prefers low h. The overlap stratum pulls **HIGH (low-h)** in the 2D channel —
per the M-2 pre-registration this **revives H-2**. The unmatched separation
(~+0.044 to +0.050 nats, perm p at floor) is mostly selection — the [A2] trap,
demonstrated, which is exactly why only the matched machinery feeds the band.

**Therefore: a detectable cross-term signature in the 2D channel is
PLAUSIBLE.** This instrument is a discovery test with a live positive
hypothesis (shared-host coherence biasing the 2D channel low-h), not a
formality expected to return zero. The band below is consciously derived so
that neither confirmation nor refutation is baked in (§7).

**M-4 destroyed the naive suppression picture (novel structural insight).**
The exact census (m4_results.json, verified CONFIRMED, 26/26 independent
checks incl. bit-identical from-scratch ball rebuilds,
`m4_adjudication_results.json`) measured that the "1/N_gal per-pair
suppression" intuition is **wrong at the per-pair level and right only at the
population level**: sharing is rare across pairs (349 of 1,260,078 event
pairs in joint_r1 1D; 2.8e-4) but **heavy within sharing pairs** — min-side
shared count share median ~0.40 (some balls near-subsets, share = 1.0),
min-side shared `w_pop` share median 0.087 (joint_r1 in-C-4), p90 0.296, max
1.00; pair-side `w_pop` shares run to p90 0.78–0.99. Tens of pairs have
O(0.1–1) shared-weight fractions. Any negligibility argument must therefore
be made at the class level with per-pair stratification (§6), never by a
blanket per-pair suppression factor. This insight stands on its own,
whichever way the instrument verdict goes.

**M-3 supplies the discipline, not the numbers.** The f_k pool substitution
was measured a pure global LEVEL (~+1.22 nats at h=0.73, event-independent to
~1e-11) with per-event chords over h ≤ 0.135 nats — two orders under its
1-nat criterion (m3_results.json; context-only, unverified, NOT
band-bearing). Lesson imported here: **only the h-chord of a correction can
tilt an H0 posterior; a level cancels in the posterior normalization.** The
decision statistic (§5) is therefore a chord across the h-grid, and the level
is reported-but-not-scored. M-3's honesty caveat is also imported: its
event-common factor still class-sums to +43.6/+48.3 nats over `combined_*`
chords — aggregates of event-common factors are recorded honestly even when
the per-event criterion passes.

