## 8. Instrument readiness — **NOT READY; run BLOCKED** (validity criteria)

**Required for validity: dual-CONFIRMED adversarial verdicts on the exact
build that runs.** Actual status at draft time:

| check | status |
|---|---|
| Original adversarial math review | **DEFECTIVE** (`instrument_math_review_20260805.json`, DEFECT-1..5) — on the PRE-fix build |
| Fix applied | yes, in place, this session (DEFECT-1/2/3/5 fixed, DEFECT-4 covered by rebuilt tests) |
| Toy suite | **15/15 PASSED** (`test_crossterm_toy.py`, incl. the previously-untested n_shared≥2 σ_z→0 pair-level limit, 2D shared-latent-M closed form vs nested quad, superset balls, floor constant) |
| Fixer's rerun of the reviewer's constructions | ALL FOUR PASS (`reviewer_checks_rerun_fixed.py/.json`: A abs diff 2.8e-15; B tracks brute-force truth at every σ_z with correct sign, O(σ²) ratios → 0.25; C nullspace universes separated 10.32%, both match truth to ~7e-16; D closed form exact at all reviewer triples) — **self-check by the fixing session, not an independent verdict** |
| Post-fix independent math re-review (round 1) | `rereview_round1_independent_checks.json`: N1–N9 **all pass** (own brute force, incl. nonconstant w_pop, unequal windows, z-dependent μ_cond nested quad, rescale invariance, mixture identity) — **no formal CONFIRMED verdict token recorded** |
| Post-fix independent numerics re-review (round 1) | `rr1_toy_attacks / rr1_boundary_check / rr1_ball_sigma_census / rr1_worst_R_table .json`: cancellation stability, invariance, guards, floor all pass, **but one real adequacy finding left OPEN (R-2 below)** — **no formal CONFIRMED verdict token recorded** |

**Verdict recorded per the validity rule: the post-fix build is NOT
dual-CONFIRMED. The instrument is NOT READY. No production run — including
smoke runs — is authorized until every blocker below is closed and this file
is ratified.**

Blockers:

- **R-1 (dual confirmation):** both post-fix adversarial re-reviewers must
  record explicit CONFIRMED/REFUTED verdicts on the frozen build (their check
  outputs pass, but a pass-list is not a verdict; the verdict must name the
  code sha256 it certifies).
- **R-2 (quadrature adequacy — the numerics reviewer's open finding):**
  `fixed_quad n=50` degrades when R = event-window-width/σ_z exceeds ~30
  (measured calibration: R≤30 → <3e-9 nats; R=45 → 3e-5; R=69 → 3e-3;
  R=110 → 6e-2, undiluted single-galaxy scale; toy mixed-ball contamination
  up to ~0.03 nats). Production census (`rr1_worst_R_table.json`): exactly
  **one** shared-galaxy instance above R=45 — joint_r1/1D pair (114, 1035),
  catalog_index 1349264, σ_z=0.0019636, R=68.17 at max window (n_shared=8861
  in that pair). σ_z=0 catalogue rows (6284 in the parent) would NaN-poison
  but **zero** appear in any ball or shared set (verified). Remedy (elevated
  quad_n for narrow kernels — n=400 measured sufficient at the worst
  geometry — or a documented per-row error budget) must be fixed, verified,
  and folded into R-1's certification **before** the run. Until then any
  Δ̃ involving that pair is numerically untrusted at the 3e-3-nat scale.
- **R-3 (target-set ingestion):** the CLI enumerates pairs only via
  `c4_pair_census`; a pair-list input consuming the §3 M-4 census (sha256-
  pinned `m4_results.json`) must be added and verified (the ingestion path
  only — the math core is untouched), then covered by R-1's certification.
- **R-4 (validate mode never run):** `--mode validate` (Step-2 N_g vs
  frozeng per-galaxy stored rows at production quad_n=50) is built but has
  never run; instrument-vs-production N replication fidelity is untested
  end-to-end. **Mandated as the FIRST gated execution after ratification**,
  before the instrument proper. Pass: max rel deviation ≤ 1e-6 over checked
  galaxies with R ≤ 30; any R > 30 galaxy is excluded from that criterion and
  handled under R-2. The emitted `S_i_frozeng/S_j_frozeng` row fields
  additionally give a free per-row own-quad-vs-production cross-check at
  readout (loader row structure validated against the real iiib
  `h_0_73.json`: keys == ball sets, 1588 events, 0 mismatches).
- **R-5 (author ratification):** every ⚑ item: §3 supersession + code-fact
  adjudication (`get_redshift_outer_bounds` hardcoded 3σ), §5 mixture-level
  band target + statistic definition, §7.2 channel choice for X, §7.4
