### §7.4 completion — per-unit 2D denominators (from the discharged flag-(e) blind read)

The draft's §7.4 table marked the 2D rows "pending" with the formula locked
(x = X/W, y = Y/W; X = 2.78, Y = 7.96). `outside_c4_2d_wpop.json` supplies the
missing outside-C-4 min-side shared w_pop share sums; the in-C-4 parts
reproduce `band_derivation.json` (joint_r1 rel 1e-12; iiib exact). Arithmetic:

| venue/channel | n pairs | W = W_in + W_out (min-side w_pop share sum) | x = X/W | y = Y/W |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| joint_r1 / 2D | 104 | 1.967897399 (27 in-C-4) + 2.127022452 (77 outside) = **4.094919851** | **0.678890** | **1.943872** |
| iiib / 2D | 21 | 0.309291700 (5 in-C-4) + 0.355208154 (16 outside) = **0.664499854** | **4.183598** | **11.978934** |

(Arithmetic: x = 2.78/4.094919851 = 0.678890; y = 7.96/4.094919851 =
1.943872; x = 2.78/0.664499854 = 4.183598; y = 7.96/0.664499854 =
11.978934.)

Interpretation note carried from the blind read: the outside-C-4 2D
population is weaker-sharing per pair (min-side median ~0.0056 vs 0.098/0.062
per-side in-C-4 medians) but its aggregate W_out slightly EXCEEDS W_in at
joint_r1 (2.127 vs 1.968) — the §6 stratum-4 (in-C-4 vs outside) split stays
load-bearing.

